    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000000": {
      "name": "08:40, and a mountain moved",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 12.0,
        "extent": [
          9498532.138560558,
          3269579.387709147,
          9541642.622513851,
          3301338.972961972
        ],
        "transition": {
          "type": "immediate",
          "time": 0.0
        },
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
            "visible": true,
            "opacity": 0.25
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
            "visible": true,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          },
          {
            "targetLayer": "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
            "visible": false,
            "opacity": 1.0
          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**At about 08:40 on 26 August 2026, roughly a square kilometre of rock and ice\ncame off a north-facing slope above the Lhende Khola, twenty kilometres upstream\nof the Nepal-China border.**\n\nIt did not stay a landslide. It picked up the loose sediment in front of a\nretreating glacier and turned into something with far more water in it than\nrock: a debris flow that went down the valley as a wall.\n\nA seismometer recorded a signal larger than magnitude 5. That was the mountain\nmoving, not an earthquake that moved it.\n\nWhat followed ran **210 km** down four rivers in a single day,\nand by the time it reached the Ganga plain it had killed **987\npeople** that anyone has found.\n\nThis map is what the flood did, put together from what the satellites saw and\nwhat Nepal's disaster authority counted.\n\n*Scroll to begin.*\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "08:40, and a mountain moved"
        }
      }
    },
