          }
        ],
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**At 08:50 the hydrological station at Syafrubesi stopped transmitting. Its last\nreading was 1.62 m.**\n\nBy **09:15** the Department of Hydrology and Meteorology had confirmed a flood\nwave and issued warnings down the Trishuli. **679,295 SMS** went out\nthrough Nepal Telecom and Ncell.\n\nFor everyone above the gauge, the warning came after the water.\n\n**On the map:** red dots are what was later marked destroyed\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Ten minutes later the gauge went quiet"
        }
      }
    },
    "2c7f4b20-0000-4000-8001-000000000003": {
      "name": "The steep gorge",
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
