          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Forty kilometres on the bed has flattened to 24.3 m per km and the valley\nhas opened out.**\n\nThe same sized box holds **490** marked destroyed. Less violent ground, but far\nmore built on it: in Nuwakot alone **1,267\nhouses** were fully damaged and **1,253**\npartially.\n\n**On the map:** the orange reach · the blue fill is the observed water line\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "The middle valley"
        }
      }
    },
